hadiths[151]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3415","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that breaking the bone of a dead person is like breaking the bone of a living person."
"3416","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: The hand of a thief will not be cut off for stealing something less than the value of a shield. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa was asked: What is the value of a shield? So he replied: A quarter of a dinar This statement of Sayyida Aisha has been narrated with reference to another chain of transmission: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The theft of a quarter of a dinar or something worth more will be cut off."
"3417","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, \The thief's hand will be cut off if he steals anything worth a quarter of a dinar or more.\"""""
"3418","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a shield or something as valuable as its value will be cut off for theft. Sulaiman bin Yasar says: The hand will be cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more (stealing something of value)."
"3419","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) cut off his hand for stealing a shield worth three dirhams."
"3420","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: During the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man stole a shield worth five dirhams, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off his hand."
"3421","Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather: In the time of the Holy Prophet, the cost of a shield was ten dirhams."
"3422","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: In those days, the price of a shield was ten dirhams. Ata says: In those days, the price of a shield was ten dirhams."
"3423","Waleed narrates that I was told by a listener from Ata, may God have mercy on him, that the price of a shield used to be ten dirhams in those days."
"3424","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the price of a shield was ten dirhams."
"3425","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the price of a shield was ten dirhams."
"3426","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the price of a shield was ten dirhams."
"3427","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: In those days, the price of a shield was ten dirhams."
"3428","Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: For the theft of (at least) ten dirhams, the hand of the thief will be cut off."
"3429","Along with another chain of transmission, it is narrated: The theft of (something of value) less than the value of the shield will not be punished (says the narrator) The value of the shield was ten dirhams."
"3430","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: In the time of the Holy Prophet, the cost of a shield was ten dirhams."
"3431","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3432","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The hand will not be cut off for anything worth less than ten dirhams."
"3433","The same hadith is also narrated along with a chain of transmission. It is chained with reference to a chain of transmission: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had his hand cut off for stealing five dirhams (of something of value)."
"3434","Sayyiduna Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Whoever prays the Isha prayer after performing ablution well and then performs four rak'ahs (Nawafil) in which he performs complete bowing and prostration, and he knows what he is praying in them, he will get the reward of performing these rak'ahs on the night of Qadr. This hadith has been narrated by Ata on the authority of Ayman, on the authority of Sa'i Yatbi. The narrator named Ayman is the one who has narrated this about the Prophet (peace be upon him) (in the time of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him))."
"3435","Abdul Wahid bin Ayman has mentioned him regarding his father. Both Ata and Mujahid have narrated hadiths regarding his father:"
"3436","Amr bin Shuaib narrates the statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about something that is found in a residential area or a common passage, and he said: \You should announce it for a year"," if its owner comes"," then it is fine"," otherwise it will be yours.\"" Al-Mal) is required to be paid. The narrator narrates) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lost goat"," and he said: Catch it because either you will find it or one of your brothers will find it or the wolf will find it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lost camel"," and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it alone"," its feet and its belly are with it"," it will reach water by itself and eat (leaves of) trees. (The narrator says) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the one who stole from the mountain"," and he said"," “Let him be beaten well"," and he shall be punished twice.” He said: If dates are stolen from a drying place"," and the value of the stolen goods is equal to a shield"," then the hand will be cut off"," and if it is less than that"," then (the thief) will be beaten and he will be charged."""
"3437","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off his hand for stealing a piece of iron worth twenty-one dirhams."
"3438","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever treats someone and he is not a physician (and the patient is harmed due to his treatment), then that person will pay the ransom."
"3439","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever treats someone and he is not a physician (and the patient suffers loss of life or less due to his treatment), that person will pay the ransom. The same hadith is narrated as Mursal, a hadith with reference to another Sunnah."
"3440","Sayyiduna Bara (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I met my maternal uncle. I inquired: He said: Are you going? He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has sent me to a man who has married his father's wife. The Prophet (peace be upon him) has instructed me to behead him."
"3441","Sayyiduna Bara' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a person to a person who had married his father's wife to behead that person."
"3442","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person belonging to the tribe of Islam came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he testified about himself four times that he had an illicit relationship with a woman. He said yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired, (in such a way that) your private parts entered into his private parts like a stitch goes into a head-dress or a dowel goes into a well. He said yes. Allah (swt) asked what do you want by this? He replied, I want you to purify me, so he was stoned to death under the order of the Holy Prophet. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard two men among his Companions talking. One of them said to the other: Look at this man. Allah kept his veil, but he himself did not let him stay and he was stoned like a dog. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. Both of them said, O Messenger of Allah, we are here. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Come down here, both of you have to take your share of meat from this dead donkey. They both said, O Messenger of Allah, may Allah forgive you, who will eat its meat? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The attack you have made on your brother's honor a little while ago is more serious than eating a dead body. By the One in whose hand is my life"," that person is taking a dip in the rivers of Paradise at that time.\"""""
"3443","Ibad bin Tamim narrates the statement of his uncle, who participated in the Battle of Badr: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a slave girl commits adultery, flog her, if she commits adultery again, flog her, if she commits it again, flog her, and sell her again, even if it is for a rope."
"3444","Sayyidna Mugheera bin Shuba (RA) narrates: A woman struck her husband with the wood of a tent, and the other woman was pregnant. The narrator narrates that one of the two women belonged to Banul Hiyan, so the Prophet (PBUH) imposed the payment of the dowry of the slain woman on the family of the murdered woman and ordered the payment of the ransom for the child in the womb of the slain woman. He who has neither eaten nor drunk anything, who has not cried (that is, has not been born), such blood goes in vain. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said, \Are you talking like the villagers?\"" The narrator says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made it obligatory to pay the dowry."""
"3445","Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates: There were two women, one of them killed the other with a wooden marker, so the Prophet (PBUH) imposed the payment of the dowry of the murdered woman on the family of the murdered woman and ordered the payment of the ransom for the child in the womb of the murdered woman. Then a villager said: Shall I pay the ransom? Whoever did not eat or drink did not scream and cry, such blood goes in vain. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said, \You are talking like a villager. The Prophet"," peace and blessings of God be upon him"," made it necessary to pay the ransom for the child in the woman's womb.\"""""
"3446","Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates: A man belonging to the Huzail tribe had two wives. One of them killed the child in her stomach by pelting the other with a stone or perhaps with a tent wood. He who did not shout and cry (i.e. was not born), who did not drink anything, did not eat anything, or recited similar words, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Are you talking like the villagers?\"" The narrator says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made it obligatory for the relatives of this woman to pay the ransom."""
"3447","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates: (In Madinah) Banu Qurayza and Banu Nazir were two clans. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent to Madinah, a man from Banu Nadir killed a man from Banu Qurayzah. Banu Qurayzah said: Hand him over to us, so that we may kill him (as revenge). They said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, is between us and you. This verse was revealed: \When you have to decide"," decide between them with justice"," the reward of life is life.\"""""
"3448","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has given this decision regarding the schools: he will have the rate of payment according to the contract of writing, according to the calculation, his duet will be the duet of a free person, and whatever payment remains on him, his duet will be the same as the duet of a slave."
"3449","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The extent to which a person is free will be considered as a free person, and the extent to which he is a slave will be considered as a slave."
"3450","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, says: Among the Children of Israel, there was a decree of retribution, but there was no decree of death among them, so Allah said to this Ummah: \Retribution has been decreed for you regarding the slain"," the free for the free"," the free for the slave"," the slave for the woman"," and whoever is forgiven by his brother.\"" Forgiveness here means that the other person is ready to accept the death penalty in the case of willful murder. That is"," it is a reduction compared to the order that was imposed on the people before you"," so Allah has given you a reduction in regard to it. You have received this reduction from your Lord."""
"3451","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \If a person peeps into someone's house without asking permission"," and he (the owner of the house) pokes something in the eye of that (peeping) person with a sharp knife"," then there will be no retribution or retribution.\"""""
"3452","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: For ten dirhams (theft of something of value) the hand will be cut off and no mahr will be less than ten dirhams."
"3453","Mu'awiya bin Qura'ah narrates this statement from his father: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, sent a man to a man who had married his father's wife to behead him."
"3454","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: A woman who apostatizes will be given respite and will not be killed."
"3455","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says about a woman who apostatizes, she will be kept alive."
"3456","Ibn Abi Khaytmah narrates: Yahya bin Mu'in says: Sufyan al-Thawri used to object to Imam Abu Hanifah because of a hadith which Imam Abu Hanifah has narrated from Abu Razin regarding Asim and no one else has narrated it except Imam Abu Hanifah."
"3457","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says about an apostate woman: She will be imprisoned and not killed."
"3458","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When women become apostates, they will not be killed."
"3459","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says about the apostate woman that she will be kept alive. Abu Asim says: Imam Abu Hanifa narrated this hadith regarding Asim, but I did not note it, I said: This tradition has been narrated to us regarding Sufyan, that is sufficient for us. Abu Asim says: We believe that Sufyan Al-Thawri has conspired with Imam Abu Hanifa in his death, so I have noted it regarding both of them."
"3460","Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) says: In Damiya, payment of a camel is required. In Baa'ah, two camels are required to be paid. In Mutalahma, three camels are required to be paid. One-third payment will be required. When a person loses his mind as a result of killing him, it will be necessary to pay the full dowry. If (as a result of this multiplication) he coughs (with Yahch) and speaks in such a way that he does not understand what he is saying, then in that case the payment of the full dowry will be required. In case of injury to the eyelid, payment of one-fourth of the dayat will be required. In case of wounding the tip of the breast, payment of one-fourth of the doyet will be required."
"3461","Narrated Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala: He heard a member of the Leprosy tribe narrate this, he narrated this with reference to Adi, a member of his tribe: Sayyidna Adi stoned his wife as a result of which the woman died. and you will not inherit it."
"3462","Arwa narrated: When Marwan bin Huqam was the governor of Madinah, a person was brought before him who used to pick up children and sell them in some other place. His hand was cut off under the order of the Holy Prophet. Marwan also ordered the same about the child stealer and that person's hand was also cut off. Abdullah Bin Muhammad is unique in narrating this tradition from Hisham and he has made many mistakes (in narrating traditions) regarding Hisham."
"3463","Saeed Bin Musayyib says: A person was killed in Sana'a (Yemen city), then Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) had seven people killed in exchange for him, and he said, \If all the people living in Sana'a had participated in the killing of that person"," I would have killed all of them instead of that person.\"""""
"3464","Narrated Ubaidullah bin Umayrah: There was a man from Sana'a who used to come (home) before the people every year. One day he returned to his house and found seven men drinking with his maidservant (or wife). They caught him and killed him and threw him into a well. When the next person came and inquired about the first person, they said that he had already left. The person who came) went to relieve himself, and he saw some flies coming from the mill of the well, from which he realized that there was meat in it. He would have killed."
"3465","Sayyidna Safwan bin Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I was sleeping on my cloak in the mosque. The cloak was worth thirty dirhams. A man came and took it from under me, (and tried to steal it). I will sell it and borrow its value (i.e. I will receive it later)."
"3466","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyidna Safwan bin Umayyah Radiyallahu Anhu was sleeping in the mosque and his cloak was under his head. A thief came and took off that cloak. Then this thief was brought to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. He confessed the crime, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, ordered his hand to be cut off. will The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Why didn't you think about this before bringing him to me?\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," recommend to forgive the criminal until the matter reaches the ruler or the judge. When it reaches the ruler and the ruler forgives him"," then Allah will not forgive the ruler."""
"3467","Hisham bin Arwah narrates this statement of his father: Sayyiduna Zubair made intercession about a thief, and someone said: First let this case be brought before the judge and then he will make intercession. So Sayyiduna Zubair said: When it reaches the judge, then Allah will curse the one who intercedes and the one to whom intercession (i.e. whoever accepts it) will be cursed, as the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said."
"3468","Farafsa Hanafi narrates: Some people took a thief with them and passed by Sayyidna Zubair (RA). He said: There is nothing wrong with it, until the matter is presented before the judge, when it is presented before the judge, Allah will not forgive him, even if the judge forgives him."
"3469","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: Sayyidna Safwan bin Umayyah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a person who had stolen his halah (the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace), then he said, O Messenger of Allah, consider (that halah on my behalf) as haba (and do not punish him) then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Why not?"
"3470","Hussain bin Munzar narrates: I was present with Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him, and Waleed bin Uqbah was brought before him. Hamran and another person testified against Waleed. Sayyidna Uthman said to Sayyidna Ali: Sayyidna Ali said to Hasan, Sayyidna Hasan said: Let the one who has this responsibility do this. He said: Stop now, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave forty lashes (to the drinker). A narrator named Abdul Aziz has narrated these words in his tradition: Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) and Sayyidna Umar (RA) inflicted eight lashes, each of them is Sunnah (i.e. permissible), but I prefer it (punishment of forty lashes)."
"3471","Narrated by Nafi: A slave of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar ran away, he passed by some of the slaves of Sayyida Aisha, he stole a bag from those slaves, which contained dates, then he rode on the donkey of those slaves and ran away. Saeed said: I will not cut off the hand of a fugitive slave. Then Sayyida Aisha sent a message to (Ibn Umar) that my slaves are also your slaves. That slave was hungry (so he stole a bag of dates)."
"3472","Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: On the occasion of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this in his sermon: The \explained\"" wound will be five"," five (camels)."""
"3473","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (From a social point of view), let the people of status pass through the gates, but the ruling of the limits is different (the limits will be extended to them)."
"3474","Sayyidna Abu Barda bin Nayar (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying that more than ten lashes should be inflicted only within the boundaries."
"3475","Ibn Muhairiz narrates: I asked Fazala bin Ubayd: What do you think about hanging a thief's hand around his neck, is it a Sunnah? He replied, \Yes"," a thief was brought to the service of the Holy Prophet"," upon the command of the Prophet"," his hand was cut off"," and then upon the command of the Prophet"," that hand was hung around his neck.\"""""
"3476","Hamza bin Abdullah narrates this statement from his father: Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab used to flog (accusation of adultery) as punishment."
"3477","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab used to issue a complete ban on (accusing adultery) as tareez."
"3478","Mu'awiya bin Qura narrated: A person said to another person: O son of a woman who smells a man's private parts (i.e. a woman who commits adultery)! So Sayyidna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) caught him, he said: I have taken this meaning by him."
"3479","Umrah narrates: There was an argument between two men and one of them said: My mother was not an adulteress and my father was not an adulteress. Sayyiduna Umar (RA) consulted the people about this, so they said: This man has praised his father and mother (that they were not adulterers). Apply"
"3480","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Amr bin Hazm to Najran, his letter also contained the following: ``Death for each tooth will be five camels, deat for all fingers will be ten, ten camels, deat for ear will be fifty camels, deat for eye will be fifty camels, deat for feet will be fifty camels, if the nose is cut off from the hump (i.e. the whole nose) then it will be full deat, in mumoma, wound, one-third of the deat of life should be given, and in the deet of Jaifa, one should pay one-third of deat of life."
"3481","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him to Yemen, he wrote to him in a letter: \When the nose is cut off from the hump"," full deed shall be paid for it"," half deed shall be paid for the eye (for loss)"," half deed shall be paid for the foot"," jaifah"," one third deed shall be paid for the wound"," mamuma"," one third deet shall be paid for the wound"," Manqla"," the wound shall be paid for fifteen camels. Each of them) will have ten camels."""
"3482","Abdullah bin Abu Bakr narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Five camels will be required to be paid in the case of an \explained\"" wound"," Mamoma"," one-third of the duet will be required"," Manqla"," fifteen camels will be required to be paid"," fifty camels will be required to be paid in the eye"," when the nose is cut off from the hump"," full duet will be required"," the tooth will be five camels"," the foot will be fifty camels"," and each of the fingers and toes will be ten camels."""
"3483","Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, decreed the payment of five camels for wounds, while he decreed the payment of five camels for teeth and the payment of ten camels for each finger."
"3484","Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had decided to pay ten ten camels in his fingers. Shu'ba narrated a hadith from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Ghalib, on the authority of Masrooq, on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, and did not mention the narrator named Hameed. Shuba has mentioned in it that Ghalib heard hadiths from Masrooq."
"3485","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \All fingers are equal.\"" A narrator named Shuba narrates: I inquired (of each of them) that ten camels would be ten. He replied yes. Abu Na'im Affan"," Muslim and other narrators have narrated it in the same way. Wakiy"," Wahib bin Jarir"," narrated by Abu Nazr on the authority of Shu'ba."""
"3486","Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the fingers (each of them being equal) will be ten camels."
"3487","Narrated by Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The fingers of the hand and the toes are equal"," each of them will have the weight of ten camels.\"""""
"3488","Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision about the fingers (their allowance) would be ten camels."
"3489","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision about the fingers, (their diet) will be ten camels. A narrator named Abu Ash'ath is unique in narrating it and according to me it is not safe to narrate it from Qatadah, Allah knows best."
"3490","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: The value of all the fingers, whether of the hands (fingers) or of the feet (the value of the fingers of each of them), will be ten camels or ten camels in terms of gold and silver."
"3491","Hajiya bin Adi narrates: Sayyiduna Ali (RA) had cut the hands of these people at the joints and (to stop the flow of blood) had put stains on them."
"3492","Narrated Sha'bi: Sayyiduna Ali used to cut off the feet but leave the heel so that the man could support it."
"3493","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: I testify about Sayyidna Umar (RA) that he cut off the hands and feet of a thief."
"3494","Abd al-Rahman bin Qasim narrates the statement of his father: Sayyidna Abu Bakr (RA) intended to cut off (the second) foot (of the thief). One hand and one foot had already been cut off."
"3495","Narrated by Saeed bin Musaib: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a person kills his father, then kill him (as revenge)."
"3496","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words added: I mentioned this tradition to Sufyan al-Thawri, and he said: I have heard this hadith from Abu Hazim, Abu Muhammad bin Sa’id also mentioned it in the same way that I did not hear it from Yahan, that this tradition was narrated from Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Mukhrami."
"3497","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \Injuring an animal will be in vain"," the blood of one who falls into a well and dies in vain"," the blood of one who dies by being buried in a mineral mine will be wasted"," and the blood of one who dies by being kicked (by an animal) will be in vain. In Raqaz"," one-fifth will be required to be paid.\"" The narrator has similarly mentioned the beating of the feet (of an animal) but this is an illusion and no one has followed him in the transmission of this word from Shu'ba."""
"3498","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The owner of a camel that damages it during the night will pay for it, but the owner of the camel will not pay for the damage that it causes during the day. (If they then cause any harm) then their feet will be cut off."
"3499","Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates: I heard Sayyidna Abul Qasim, the Prophet of Repentance, (PBUH) saying, “Whoever falsely accuses a slave under his possession of adultery, and he (the slave) is innocent of what he has accused, then Allah will punish the accuser on the Day of Resurrection with as many lashes as possible. is)."
"3500","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of Sayyidna Abul Qasim, the Prophet of Repentance, (PBUH) who falsely accuses his slave of adultery and he is acquitted of what he has accused, then Allah will punish the accuser on the Day of Resurrection with the same whipping."
"3501","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled about the nose that if it is cut off completely, its deet will be complete (as much as the deet of the whole soul) and if the front part of it is cut off, its deet will be half."
"3502","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: (the penalty for cutting off) the forty hands will be one-third of the duet, and if the eye has lost its light but is still in its place, then one-third of the duet will be required."
"3503","The son of Sayyidna Khuzima bin Thabit Ansari narrates this statement of his father: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Whoever commits a punishable crime and is punished"," it will be an atonement for his sin.\"""""
"3504","The son of Sayyidna Khuzima bin Thabit Ansari narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Whoever commits a crime and then is punished for that crime"," then it will be expiation for him.\"""""
"3505","It is narrated along with the same document that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever commits an act that Allah has forbidden, and then a limit is issued to that person, then it will be an atonement for the sinner.” A narrator named Osama bin Zayd has followed both of them in narrating it."
"3506","Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to us: Pledge my allegiance on this matter. You will not associate anyone with Allah. You will not steal. You will not commit adultery. You will not kill your children. Whoever among you fulfills this (covenant) will be rewarded by Allah Almighty. Whoever commits one of these crimes and is punished for it, it will be an atonement for him."
"3507","Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I pledged allegiance to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with a few of my companions. Allah will reward him, and whoever commits one of these crimes, i.e. the limit of it will be extended to him, it will be a cause of purification for him, and whoever Allah hides, his case will be in the hands of Allah."
"3508","Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) who participated in the Battle of Badr and is one of the Naqba of the Night of Uqbah, narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (after that he mentioned the previous hadith). However, it contains these words: Whoever commits one of these crimes and is punished for it in this world, it will be expiation for him."
"3509","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, “Whoever commits a sin in this world and is punished for it, the glory of Allah is greater than that He punishes that person again, and whoever commits a sin in this world and Allah covers it and forgives him, then the glory of Allah is greater than that He punishes him again for what He has already forgiven.”"
"3510","Qasim narrates that Sayyidna Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, after cutting off the hand and foot (of a thief) wanted to cut off the other foot (for his third theft), then Sayyidna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Sunnah is that (now) the hand should be cut off."
"3511","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: In the era of Jahiliyya, there were four ways of marriage. One way of marriage was the one that is common among people today. Send a message and have intercourse with her, that person was separated from his wife during that time, and did not have intercourse with her wife until the pregnancy of the woman with whom the woman had intercourse was revealed to the other person, when the pregnancy of the woman was revealed, her real husband would have intercourse with her if he wanted, he did it so that his child would be the sperm of a member of a large family, the name of this marriage is Nikah Istba'ah. It was given. Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The third method of marriage was that when some people gathered, their number was less than ten, they all went to a woman and they all had intercourse with her, then she would get pregnant and finally give birth to a child. was I have given birth to a child, O so-and-so! This is your son, if that woman were to name the person whom she wanted, then her child's lineage would be established with that person, that person could no longer deny this child. The fourth method was that many people would go together to a woman. That woman could not stop anyone who came to her. These women used to be prostitutes. They used to have special flags on their doors. There was a symbol of the young man's profession. The person who wanted to go to them would call. would place his child with the person, with whom that child resembled, then people would call that child as that person's son and that person could not deny it."
"3512","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that there were four types of marriages during the time of Jahiliyyah (after that she has mentioned according to the previous hadith). In one tradition, these words are added: (The husband would say to his wife) You send a message to such and such a person, then you have intercourse with him. During this time, the husband of this woman would stay away from her and would not have intercourse with the woman until the person with whom the woman had intercourse became pregnant. had gone The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, but the names are these words (the husband would say to his wife:) You send a message to such and such a person and get pregnant from him. Muhammad bin Ishaq narrates: It is true (it also contains these words:) When Allah sent Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the truth, He abolished the nikah (various methods of marriage) of the age of ignorance."
"3513","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: In the time of Jahiliyyah, a person used to say to another, “You let me have intercourse with your wife, I will let you have intercourse with my wife, and I will give you more (benefits).” So Allah revealed this verse: The narrator narrates: Sayyidna Uyaina bin Hisn al-Fazari, may God bless him and grant him peace, attended the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was present with Sayyida Aisha, may God bless him and grant him peace. At that time, Ayyaena entered without seeking permission. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: O Ayyaena, why did you not take permission? He said, O Messenger of Allah, since I became an adult, I have not asked permission to enter from any member of the dangerous tribe. He also said: Who is this beautiful lady by your side? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is Aisha, the mother of all believers. He said: Shall I not replace her and give you a more beautiful woman? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, O Ayyna! Allah Ta'ala has declared this act as haram. The narrator says) When that person left, Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) inquired, O Messenger of Allah, who was this? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He was a foolish leader, you have seen his (mental state) yet he is the leader of his people."
"3514","Abu Barda quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding his father: There is no marriage without a guardian."
"3515","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3516","Abd al-Rahman Hamzani, in his chain of transmission, has quoted it from Israel as Ibn Sinan has quoted it. Muhammad Ibn Mukhlid says: Abd al-Rahman said to Hamzani: Gaya, Shu'ba and Sufyan both narrated it as a muquf, tradition up to Abu Barda, so he said: The tradition narrated by Isra'il regarding Abu Ishaq is more favorite to me than the tradition transmitted by Sufyan and Shu'ba."
"3517","Dalaj bin Ahmar has quoted this saying of Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi along with his chain of transmission: Israel remembered the traditions of Abu Ishaq in the same way that they remembered Surah Fatiha. Salih says: Israel especially (transcribes) the traditions of Abu Ishaq more safely."
"3518","Abu Barda quotes the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding his father (Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari) that there is no marriage without a guardian."
"3519","Abu Saeed says: A marriage is not valid without guardians, witnesses and dower, but the marriage of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) can also take place without them."
"3520","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that if a woman marries without the permission of a guardian, her marriage will be invalid, her marriage will be invalid, her marriage will be invalid, if a man has intercourse with her, then because of this act of the man, the woman will receive a dowry."
"3521","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A marriage cannot take place without a guardian and two just witnesses. A narrator named 'Adi bin Fazl narrated it as a Marfu' Hadith, while other narrators did not narrate it as a Marfu' Hadith."
"3522","Abu Salama narrates: I asked Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA): How much did the Prophet (PBUH) respect his wives? So Sayyida Aisha said twelve oqiyah and, Nish. Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa inquired, do you know what is meant by Nish, it means half an ounce and (the total amount of dowry) is five hundred dirhams."
"3523","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) was among us, we used to pay ten ounces of Mahr."
"3524","Sayyidna Hasan Basri says: Sayyidna Muaqal bin Yasar (RA) married his sister, her husband divorced her, I married you to my (honorable sister) and you divorced her, now you have sent a message of marriage. \When you divorce women"," and their period of marriage is completed"," do not forbid them to marry (their former) husbands. This hadith is authentic. Imam Bukhari"," may God have mercy on him"," narrated it from Yunus on the authority of Abu Muammar"," on the authority of Abdul Warith"," and on the authority of Ahmad bin Abu Amr"," on the authority of his father"," on the authority of Ibrahim bin Tahman"," on the authority of Yunus."""
"3525","Hasan al-Basri narrates about Allah's saying: So do not forbid these women to marry (their former) husbands, if they agree (to remarry) properly. Hasan al-Basri said: Sayyidna Muqal bin Yasar Muzni (may God be pleased with him) told me: This verse was revealed about him. Then you have come with the message of marriage, no! By Allah, you will never be able to get him again, Sayyiduna Muqal says: There was no other defect in this person, and that woman also wanted to marry him again, so Allah revealed this verse. (Narrated by Sayyidna Muaqal, may Allah be pleased with him) I said: O Messenger of Allah, now I will do the same, then I married the woman to this person."
"3526","Sayyidna Muqal bin Yasar (may God be pleased with him) narrates: I had a sister, some people approached her for marriage, but I forbade them, then my cousin came to me, he sent a message of marriage to this girl, so I married the girl to him, as long as Allah permitted, they both stayed together, then the person divorced the girl, in which he had room to approach, but the person did not approach, until That the girl's period has passed, after that she also sent a marriage message along with other people, so I said: I did not marry this girl to any of the other people, and I married her to you, but you divorced her, in which there was room for appeal, but you did not appeal, until her period passed, now when her relationship is coming, you also sent a relationship. The verse was revealed (the narrator doubts that perhaps these are the words) this verse was revealed. \When you divorce women and their periods are completed"," do not forbid them from remarrying (their former) husbands.\"" (Narrated by Sayyiduna Muaqal"," may Allah be pleased with him) I expiate my oath and married this girl to this person. The meaning of this narration is close (to each other)."""
"3527","Sayyidna Muqal bin Yasar (RA) narrates: My sister was the wife of a man, he divorced her until her period passed, then the person sent a message of marriage, so Sayyidna Muqal (RA) got angry at this, he said, he had left the girl even though he could have approached her. \When you divorce women and their periods are completed"," do not forbid them from remarrying.\"""""
"3528","Abd al-Rahman bin Sulaiman narrates the statement of his paternal aunt Sakina bint Hantala: Imam Hamad al-Baqir (RA) asked for permission to come to me. At that time, my husband's death had not yet passed. He said: \You are aware of my relationship with the Prophet (PBUH) and my relationship with Sayyiduna Ali (RA) and my status among the Arabs (I want to marry you). I said: O Abu Ja'far"," may God forgive you. is used"," and you are giving me a marriage message during my Idda"," so Imam Baqir (RA) said"," I told you about my relationship with the Prophet (SAW) and with Sayyiduna Ali (RA)"," when the Prophet (SAW) took Umm Salama (to give her a message of marriage) to him"," she was performing the Idda (married after the death of Sayyidna Abu Salama). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," (O Umm Salamah) you know that I am the Messenger of Allah and His chosen one and my position in my nation (you are aware of it)."""
"3529","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: Four things are necessary in a marriage: the guardian, the husband, (or wife) and the double. The narrator named Abul Hasib Nafi bin Mesra is unknown."
"3530","Narrated by Ikrama bin Khalid: I met some horsemen on the way. One of them, a Saiba woman, entrusted the matter of her marriage to a person who was not her guardian, (to marry her), so that person married her."
"3531","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \There is no marriage without valid and just witnesses.\"""""
"3532","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said, \There is no marriage without a guardian and two righteous witnesses.\"""""
"3533","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Marriage cannot take place without a guardian and two righteous witnesses. If those guardians disagree"," then the one who has no guardian"," the ruler of time is his guardian.\"" This tradition is narrated along with some other isnads"," but there are some word differences in it."""
"3534","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \There is no marriage without a guardian and two righteous witnesses.\"""""
"3535","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \No woman should marry another woman"," no woman can marry herself. A woman who commits adultery marries herself.\"""""
"3536","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said, \No woman should marry another woman; no woman can marry herself.\"" (The narrator says) We said: We used to say: A woman who marries herself is a fajra (adulteress"," evildoer)."""
"3537","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3538","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: We used to say that a woman who marries herself is an adulteress."
"3539","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: No woman can marry another woman, no woman can marry herself, an adulterous woman can marry herself without the permission of her guardian."
"3540","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No woman can marry another woman, no woman can marry herself, a prostitute does her own marriage. A narrator named Ibn Sirin narrates: Sometimes Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) used the word Zania for her."
"3541","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates as a hadith: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No woman can marry another woman, nor can a woman marry herself."
"3542","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, says: A woman can marry only with the permission of her guardian (if she is not a guardian), then she can marry with the permission of a wise person of her family or the ruler of the time."
"3543","Sha'bi narrated: In the matter of marrying (a woman) without a guardian, the most strict among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), he used to punish (committing this act)."
"3544","Syedna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that marriage does not take place without the permission of a guardian."
"3545","It has been narrated about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): He married the daughter of his uncle Sayyidna Uthman Bin Mazoon (RA). Sayyidna Ibn Umar (RA) narrates: The father of this girl came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and said, “My daughter dislikes this relationship.” The Prophet (PBUH) instructed Ibn Umar (RA) to divorce her. Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him, separated from him. The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said, \Do not marry girls until their opinion is known. If they remain silent (in response)"," it will be their permission.\"" The narrator narrates: Later"," Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) married this girl. A narrator named Ibn Abi Wahhab has not heard it from Nafi"," he has narrated it from Nafi on the authority of Umar bin Husain."""
"3546","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: My uncle, Sayyidna Qudama bin Maz’un (RA) married the daughter of his brother Sayyidna Uthman bin Maz’un (RA) to me. O Messenger of Allah, this is my niece. I am her father's heir. I did not abuse this girl. I married her to a person whose virtues and kinship (to us) you are also aware of. The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said, \She is a girl"," and a girl is more entitled to her own affairs.\"" got married Shaykh says: Muhammad bin Ishaq did not hear this tradition from Nafi"," he heard it from Umar bin Hussain. Ibrahim ibn Sa'd has narrated this tradition in the same way on his account"," while Muhammad ibn Salama has followed it on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq as being transmitted from Umar ibn Husain."""
"3547","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Uthman bin Mazoun (RA) died, he left behind a daughter whose mother was Sayyida Khula bint Hakim. Sayyidna Uthman bin Mazoun bequeathed it to his brother Sayyidna Qudama bin Mazoun. These two gentlemen were my uncles. Then Sayyidna Mugheera (RA) went to the girl's mother and offered her more wealth, so she inclined towards him. The girl preferred her mother's wishes. The matter of these people was presented to the Prophet (PBUH), then Sayyidna Qudama said, \O Messenger of Allah"," this is my niece. My brother had bequeathed her to me. I will marry her to Ibn Umar. I will improve her and our relationship. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"," “This is a girl"," and she cannot be married without her consent.” (Ibn Umar says) “By Allah"," she had become the owner (that is"," marriage"," but because of this decree of the Prophet"," peace be upon him)"," she was separated from me"," and her family married her to Sayyidna Mughira bin Shu’bah"," may God be pleased with her.”"""
"3548","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Uthman bin Mazoun left a girl (among the survivors), my uncle Sayyidna Qudama bin Mazoun married her to me, he did not know the girl's will in this regard, he was the boy's uncle, the girl spoke to the Prophet about this, and the Prophet declared her marriage void. If they did, (the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or Sayyidna Qudama) married that girl to him (ie Sayyidna Mugheera)."
"3549","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) married his daughter Zainab bint Uthman after the death of Sayyidna Uthman bint Uthman. This marriage was arranged by the girl's uncle Sayyidna Qudama. Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba offered her a large dowry, so the girl's mother said to the girl: \Don't keep (the marriage made by her uncle).\"" Then this girl and her mother told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled this marriage."""
"3550","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: A girl should be married with her permission."
"3551","Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid (RA) and Sayyidna Majma’ bin Yazid (RA) say: Sayyidna Khuzam (RA) married his daughter, Khunsa, that woman did not like that person, she was a Thaiba (widow or divorcee)."
"3552","It is narrated about Sayyida Khansaa, may Allah be pleased with her, that she was a widow, her father married her to a man from Banuuf, she wanted to marry a woman named Abul Baba bin Abdul Mundhir, her matter was presented to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed her father to marry her according to her wishes."
"3553","Abu Salama narrates: A woman from the Ansar family of Banu Umar and Bin Awf, whose name was Khunsa bint Khudam, was married to her by her father, she was Thaiba. Married to Munzar, and had Sayyidna Abul Baba's son, Sa'ib."
"3554","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The father of Sayyida Khansa bint Khudam (RA) married her (to this husband). She disliked the woman. She came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and mentioned her matter to the Prophet (PBUH), so the Prophet (PBUH) annulled her marriage. Then Sayyidna Abul Baba Bin Abdul Manzar married her, and with her, Sayyidna Abul Baba Sahibzada, Saib, was born, the woman was a Saiba (widow or divorcee)."
"3555","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A girl came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father, who is the best of fathers, married me to his nephew so that because of me he would be inferior, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this girl the option (to annul the marriage). That the father has no authority about this."
"3556","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A girl came to him (after this the hadith is in the next hadith). Narrated by Abdullah bin Burida: A girl came to the service of Sayyida Aisha (RA) and said: \My father has married me to his nephew so that because of me his inferior status will improve. I don't like it. Sayya Aisha said"," 'You sit until the Prophet comes. I will present the matter before you.' So"," the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the girl's father"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the girl the option (of maintaining or annulling the marriage). A narrator named Ibn Junayd narrated these words: He said"," O Messenger of Allah"," I maintain what he has done."""
"3557","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A woman came to meet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not there. She sat down and waited for the Prophet (peace be upon him). Better yet, my father has not known my will in this matter, so do I have any authority over myself? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Yes","\"" said the woman"," \""I do not want to reject what my father has done"," but I want women to know that they have a choice about themselves or not.\"" Shaykh says: All these hadiths are transmissions"," because the narrator named Ibn Burida did not hear the hadiths from Sayyida Aisha."""
"3558","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates: A man married one of his virgin daughters, he did not ask the girl's permission, the girl came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and the Prophet (PBUH) annulled her marriage. A narrator named Abu Bakr has narrated these words, that girl was a virgin (and her marriage) without his permission, she came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Prophet made a separation between them."
"3559","Ata bin Abi Rabah narrates: A man married his daughter."
"3560","Ata bin Abi Rabah narrates: During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him), a man married his virgin daughter. The girl disliked the relationship. Shaykh says: It is correct that this hadith is transmitted and the statement of a narrator named Shoaib is an illusion."
"3561","Narrated by Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of the Prophet (may peace be upon him) (followed by the previous hadith) The narrator narrates this hadith on the authority of Ata, the Messenger, as a hadith, just as it is on the authority of Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"3562","Ata bin Abi Rabah narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, separated a woman from her husband, she was a virgin, her father had married her, and the woman did not like this relationship."
"3563","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled the marriage of a virgin girl and a pregnant woman. Their father married them both and they did not like (this relationship), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled their marriage. On the authority of Abu Kathir on the authority of Mahajar bin Ikrimah, it is transmitted as a messenger tradition from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"3564","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3565","Muhajar bin Ikramah has narrated a tradition similar to this regarding the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
